# Files copied from ../updater_wip into this folder, so that v1.37 stands alone (as v1.36 does), and still held to
# those bytes: sha256, the path here, the path in the repository. Copied at v137-build 820cfb20: WORKER8's link
# (updater_wip/link, last changed at b59529dd), WORKER10's wire (updater_wip/wire, db9cb7ad), gold with
# the host's frames and chapter 28's packets (updater_wip/pipeline/gold, bc85fd2e; here pipeline/frames/gold, beside
# pipeline/gold, which is v1.3's and pinned by pipeline/FROM-V1.3.sha256). tools/check_copies.sh checks them.
# Added 2026-11-19, before the freeze: the link's report and its hardware document (link/REPORT.md, link/HARDWARE.md) and
# its task generator for the runner (link/make_task.sh), all WORKER8's, from updater_wip/planning/sessions/WORKER8/;
# link/README.md copied again, its pointer to the report now right in both places; link/Makefile copied again, taking
# HARDWARE.md from beside it when it is there.
# 2026-11-19, with the freeze: updater_wip/ was removed. The third column is where each file was built, and is no
# longer a path of the repository; its planning papers are planning/updater/. Four files were changed here at
# that removal and are held to their bytes as changed: gold's three development scripts that reach ../v1.36 and
# ../v1.3 (test/frames/guests.sh, old_unchanged.sh, workloads.sh: one folder deeper here), and the wire's task
# generator (wire/tests/make_task.sh: it takes the wire's folder from where it sits).
